  "subtitle": "Dr Torun Ezeigwe and what a pass mark measures",
  "summary": "A short profile of Dr Torun Ezeigwe, Senior Lecturer and Director of the Master of Applied Measurement, told largely in her own words. When nearly everyone passes, Dr Ezeigwe goes back to the instrument, and she takes three of her own studies in turn: a first-aid checklist with nineteen of its twenty-four boxes ticked on almost every sheet, a junior umpire accreditation rate of nearly ninety-nine per cent that falls under forty on first attempts, and two assessors who agree least where a rental's deductions fall. The video also marks her place among the University's ten most published researchers.",
